# Production-build overrides (loaded by `npm run build`, not by `npm run dev`).

# Sub-path the app is hosted under. Must start AND end with "/".
# Blank, commented out, or removed = hosted at the SITE ROOT, which is what a local
# `dotnet run` and a root-bound IIS site both need.
#
# LEFT DISABLED ON PURPOSE. Setting it bakes the prefix into every asset URL, the router
# basename and the API prefix, so a build made with it produces a WHITE SCREEN anywhere that
# is not serving under that exact prefix — index.html asks for /shotsense/assets/index-*.js,
# the server has it at /assets/index-*.js, nothing loads, and the page renders empty with no
# visible error.
#
# Enable it ONLY when deploying under an IIS application alias, and make the value match the
# alias exactly (see DEPLOYMENT-NOTES.md section 3.2 / 5). Rebuild after changing it, and
# check that PLCGateway/wwwroot/index.html references the path you expect before publishing.
#
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/shotsense/
